# Rot — Full Project Walkthrough

> **Recursive Operations Tool** — A next-generation, open-source AI coding agent for your terminal, built in Rust.

---

## What Is Rot?

Rot is a **terminal-based AI coding assistant** that lets developers pair-program with LLMs directly from the command line. It's comparable to tools like Aider, Claude Code, or Cursor — but runs entirely in your terminal with a custom TUI, supports *any* LLM provider, and introduces a unique **RLM (Recursive Language Model) engine** that can process **10M+ token contexts** by recursively chunking and reasoning over massive documents.

---

## Architecture Overview

Rot is a **Rust workspace** with **11 crates**, ~96 source files, organized by clear separation of concerns:

```
rot/
├── crates/
│   ├── rot-cli          # Binary entry point, CLI arg parsing (clap)
│   ├── rot-core         # Agent loop, messages, permissions, config, security
│   ├── rot-provider     # LLM provider abstraction (7 backends)
│   ├── rot-tools        # 20 built-in tools (file ops, bash, search, etc.)
│   ├── rot-rlm          # RLM engine (recursive reasoning over massive contexts)
│   ├── rot-tui          # Terminal UI (ratatui + crossterm)
│   ├── rot-session      # JSONL session persistence with tree structure
│   ├── rot-sandbox      # OS-level sandboxing (macOS Seatbelt, Linux bwrap)
│   ├── rot-serve        # Headless HTTP API server (Axum)
│   ├── rot-mcp          # Model Context Protocol integration
│   └── rot-plugin       # Plugin system (future/stub)
├── Cargo.toml           # Workspace root (v0.1.2, Rust 2021, min 1.75)
├── architecture.md      # 2700-line technical design document
├── plan.md              # Task-by-task implementation guide
├── brainstorm.md        # Research & competitive analysis
└── pdr.md               # Product requirements document
```

### Dependency Graph

```mermaid
graph TD
    CLI["rot-cli (binary)"] --> Core["rot-core"]
    CLI --> TUI["rot-tui"]
    CLI --> Serve["rot-serve"]
    Core --> Provider["rot-provider"]
    Core --> Tools["rot-tools"]
    Core --> Session["rot-session"]
    Core --> RLM["rot-rlm"]
    Core --> Plugin["rot-plugin"]
    Core --> Sandbox["rot-sandbox"]
    Tools --> MCP["rot-mcp"]
    RLM --> Provider
```

