### 4. `rot-tools` — 20 Built-in Tools

Registered in [builtin/mod.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-tools/src/builtin/mod.rs):

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `ReadTool` | Read file contents |
| `ListTool` | List directory entries |
| `CodeSearchTool` | Semantic code search |
| `LspTool` | Language Server Protocol queries |
| `WriteTool` | Write/create files |
| `EditTool` | Targeted file edits |
| `PatchTool` | Apply patches |
| `QuestionTool` | Ask the user a follow-up question |
| `TodoReadTool` / `TodoWriteTool` | Persistent task tracking |
| `BashTool` | Execute shell commands (sandboxed) |
| `GlobTool` | Find files by glob pattern |
| `GrepTool` | Search file contents with regex |
| `TaskTool` | Delegate to a sub-agent |
| `WebFetchTool` | Fetch URLs |
| `WebSearchTool` | Web search |
| `TmuxCaptureTool` / `TmuxSendKeysTool` | Tmux integration |
| `NvimReadTool` / `NvimWriteTool` | Neovim integration |

Also supports **MCP (Model Context Protocol)** tools via [mcp.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-tools/src/mcp.rs) and **custom external tools** via [external.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-tools/src/external.rs).

Each tool implements the [Tool](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-serve/src/lib.rs#53-57) trait with JSON Schema parameter definitions, async [execute](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/engine.rs#28-34), and structured `ToolResult` output. A `PathGuard` module ([path_guard.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-tools/src/path_guard.rs)) enforces sandbox boundaries.

