### 5. `rot-rlm` — Recursive Language Model Engine

The standout feature. Key files:

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| [engine.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/engine.rs) | Main RLM loop (589 lines) |
| [repl.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/repl.rs) | Bash REPL environment |
| [python_repl.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/python_repl.rs) | Python REPL environment |
| [context.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/context.rs) | External context storage |
| [context_loader.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/context_loader.rs) | Load contexts from files/PDFs |
| [subcall.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/subcall.rs) | Sub-LLM call orchestration |
| [runtime.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/runtime.rs) | Runtime abstraction |
| [runtime_docker.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/runtime_docker.rs) | Docker-isolated execution |
| [runtime_local.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/runtime_local.rs) | Local execution |
| [trace.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/trace.rs) | Execution trajectory tracing |
| [usage.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/usage.rs) | Token usage tracking |
| [prompts.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-rlm/src/prompts.rs) | System prompts for RLM mode |

**How RLM works**: Instead of cramming a massive document into one LLM call, RLM stores the context externally in temp files, exposes it as a variable in a REPL (bash or Python), and lets the LLM write code to iteratively chunk, query sub-LLMs, filter, and aggregate — until calling `FINAL(answer)`. Think of it as giving the LLM a programmable workspace to reason recursively over unbounded data.

**Available REPL functions**: `llm_query()`, `llm_query_batched()`, `rlm_query()` (recursive), `rlm_query_batched()`, `SHOW_VARS()`, `FINAL()`, `FINAL_VAR()`.

---

### 6. `rot-sandbox` — OS-Level Sandboxing

[lib.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-sandbox/src/lib.rs) (386 lines):

- **macOS**: Uses `sandbox-exec` with Seatbelt profiles for fine-grained filesystem/network restrictions
- **Linux**: Uses `bwrap` (bubblewrap) for namespace isolation
- **Three modes**: `ReadOnly`, `WorkspaceWrite`, `DangerFullAccess`
- Supports both one-shot command execution and long-lived process spawning

---

### 7. `rot-session` — Session Persistence

- **JSONL format** — one JSON object per line
- **Tree structure** via [id](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-provider/src/traits.rs#13-39) and `parent_id` for conversation branching
- **Operations**: create, load, list, export, import, tree visualization
- Sessions stored under OS data directories (`dirs::data_dir()`)
- Auto-saved on each message

---

### 8. `rot-tui` — Terminal User Interface

[app.rs](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-tui/src/app.rs) (1720 lines) — main rendering and state:

- Built on **ratatui** + **crossterm**
- Tokyo Night-inspired color palette
- Vim keybindings (Normal/Insert mode)
- Streaming markdown rendering with inline code, bold, italic
- **Features**: model selector dialog, agent selector, slash commands, RLM toggle, access mode toggle, context window tracker, clipboard support, timer, token counter
- **Slash commands**: `/tools`, `/rlm`, `/config`, `/agents`, `/help`, `/clear`, `/session`, `/copy`, `/quit`

---

### 9. `rot-serve` — Headless HTTP API

An **Axum** server exposing rot's capabilities over HTTP:

- `GET /health` — health check
- `POST /exec` — execute a prompt (with optional provider/model/agent/session overrides)
- Returns structured JSON: response text, tool call records, usage summary, timing

---

### 10. `rot-mcp` — Model Context Protocol

Integrates external MCP servers configured in `~/.rot/config.json`. Tools from MCP servers are registered alongside built-in tools.

### 11. `rot-plugin` — Plugin System (Stub)

Reserved for future plugin/WASM extensibility.

---

## Key Design Patterns

| Pattern | Implementation |
|---------|---------------|
| **Async-first** | Tokio runtime, all I/O is async |
| **Trait-based abstraction** | [Provider](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-provider/src/traits.rs#13-39), [Tool](file:///Users/akashrathod/Desktop/projects/rot/crates/rot-serve/src/lib.rs#53-57) traits for extensibility |
| **Streaming** | SSE-based streaming from all providers, normalized to `StreamEvent` |
| **Event callbacks** | Agent emits `StreamEvent`s via callbacks for TUI real-time rendering |
| **Approval system** | `ApprovalCallback` for interactive permission prompts before tool execution |
| **OS sandboxing** | Commands run under Seatbelt (macOS) or bwrap (Linux) |
| **Task delegation** | Sub-agents via `TaskTool` with bounded iterations and separate message histories |
| **Workspace-scoped** | Sessions & path guards scoped to current working directory |

---

## Data Flow

```
User Input
    │
    ▼
rot-cli (main.rs)
    │ ── parse CLI args
    │ ── load config from ~/.rot/config.json
    │ ── create Provider, ToolRegistry, Agent
    │
    ├── Chat Mode ──► rot-tui (run_tui)
    │                    │
    │                    ▼
    │              TUI event loop
    │                    │ user types message
    │                    ▼
    │              Agent.process()
    │                    │
    ├── Exec Mode ──► Agent.process() directly
    │
    ▼
Agent Loop (rot-core/agent.rs)
    │
    ├─► Provider.stream(request)  ← rot-provider
    │       │
    │       ▼
    │   Parse StreamEvents (text, tool calls, thinking)
    │       │
    │       ├─ Text ──► emit via EventCallback ──► TUI renders
    │       │
    │       └─ ToolCall ──► check permissions ──► execute tool
    │                           │
    │                           ├─ BashTool ──► rot-sandbox
    │                           ├─ ReadTool, WriteTool, etc.
    │                           ├─ TaskTool ──► spawn sub-agent
    │                           └─ MCP tools ──► rot-mcp
    │
    │   Tool results added to messages, loop continues
    │
    └─► Session auto-saved (rot-session, JSONL)
```

---

## How to Build & Run

```bash
# Build
cargo build                    # Debug
cargo build --release          # Optimized (LTO, stripped)

# Run
cargo run --package rot-cli    # TUI chat mode
rot                            # After install

# Test
cargo test                     # All tests
cargo test --package rot-core  # Specific crate

# Lint
cargo clippy -- -D warnings
cargo fmt -- --check
```

---

## Configuration

- **Global config**: `~/.rot/config.json`
- **API keys**: via environment variables (`ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`)
- **Security**: `--sandbox` and `--ask-for-approval` flags, or config defaults
- **MCP servers**: configured in `config.json` under `mcp_servers`

